const NOB88 = `After reading the article about his death, Nobel was (A)__________ disappointed.\n"How could this be? This is unbelievable! I'm not a merchant of death. I want to (B)__________ in a different way. I want to (B)__________ as a person who made the world better."\nHe decided to change (C)<u>people's opinions</u> about him.\nIn 1888, a French newspaper mistakenly reported Alfred Nobel's death. The person who had actually died was his brother, Ludvig. Thanks to the report, however, Nobel decided to do something to contribute to the world. In 1895, he decided to use his money (D)<u>to create the Nobel Prize</u>. Originally, there were only five awards. A sixth award was added in 1968. Today, when we think of Alfred Nobel, we think of (E)______________________.`;
