const CHRIS144 = `Dear Chris,\nTwo weeks ago, I moved to a new middle school. I have been feeling like a stranger ever since. The most difficult thing about school is making friends. Sometimes I have lunch in the school cafeteria with some of the students that I got to know from the class, but most of the time, I have lunch by myself. Sometimes, I want to skip lunch rather than feel lonely and miserable. I cannot just let my school life go on like this. What should I do? I don't know what to do. I really need your advice.\nNick\n\nDear Nick,\nYou need to keep this simple rule in mind: you should ⓐ______________________. When you see people having lunch, go and ask if you can sit with them. (A)<u>Then, start a light conversation about the weather, a TV show or school life</u>. (B)<u>Such conversation makes people feel closer to each other</u>. (C)<u>You should remember it is important not to talk to others when having lunch</u>. (D)<u>You may be afraid of being rejected, but I'm sure they won't</u>. (E)<u>People are nicer than you think</u>. Think positive!\nIn order to make new friends, you have to give a good impression of yourself. Make sure you have a smile on your face at all times. Your smile will bring you many chances to make new friends. Good luck.\nChris`;
