add(R, passage(P, CHRIS144, `위 글의 빈칸 ⓐ에 들어갈 말로 알맞은 것은?`), '4', ['care about how you look to others', 'simply wait for people to come to you', 'share how you feel with the people around you', 'approach the people you want to be friends with first', 'read a lot of books about how to communicate with others']);
add(R, passage(P, CHRIS144, `위 글과 다음 Nick이 쓴 일기의 밑줄 친 ㉠~㉦ 중, 일치하지 않거나 글을 통해 알 수 없는 내용이 포함된 것의 개수는?\n\n㉠<u>I moved to a new school a few weeks ago</u>. ㉡<u>I am having a difficulty in making friends</u>. ㉢<u>When I have lunch at school, there is always no one around me</u>. ㉣<u>I feel so lonely when having lunch in the school cafeteria by myself</u>. ㉤<u>I don't want to spend my school life like this, feeling lonely</u>. ㉥<u>But I don't know how to deal with my situation</u>. ㉦<u>I asked for help to the school counselor, Chris, but I didn't get any useful advice</u>.`), '1', ['2개', '3개', '4개', '5개', '6개']);
add(R, `다음 주어진 글에 이어질 순서로 알맞은 것은?\n\nLooking back on this year, I'm glad that I donated money to children in Africa.\n\n(A) By not buying snacks for a month, I was able to save the money. I have learned an important lesson through this experience.\n(B) For example, I sometimes left food on my plate. Now I really appreciate my meals. I'm proud of myself.\n(C) I did this because I wanted to make a difference for children in need. To do so, I had to save money.`, '4', ['(A)-(B)-(C)', '(B)-(A)-(C)', '(B)-(C)-(A)', '(C)-(A)-(B)', '(C)-(B)-(A)']);

