add(R, `다음 영영풀이를 참고하여 가로 퍼즐 ⓐ~ⓖ를 각각 완성했을 때, 세로 퍼즐 (A)에 해당하는 단어의 영영풀이로 알맞은 것은?\n(그림 설명: 가로 퍼즐 ⓐ~ⓖ의 답을 채우면 세로 (A) 칸에 한 단어가 만들어진다. 세로 (A)는 각 가로 단어의 다음 글자를 위에서 아래로 읽은 것이다: ⓐ의 1번째 글자, ⓑ의 5번째 글자, ⓒ의 4번째 글자, ⓓ의 4번째 글자, ⓔ의 6번째 글자, ⓕ의 5번째 글자, ⓖ의 4번째 글자.)\n\n[ACROSS]\nⓐ to gain a goal or point in a sport or game\nⓑ a person who sells products in large amounts\nⓒ to give information about something in a newspaper or on TV or radio\nⓓ to say what someone or something is like\nⓔ not on purpose\nⓕ to be grateful for something\nⓖ the title written in large letters over a story in a newspaper`, '2', ['a powerful explosive', 'in a state of great surprise', 'to feel sorry or unhappy about something', 'unhappy because something you hoped for did not happen', 'a ceremony at which degrees or diplomas are given out']);
add(R, `다음 중 어법상 알맞은 것은?`, '2', ['When I had woke up, the rain already stops.', 'He had stayed up late until his family returned.', 'I had gone to school after I took a shower quickly.', "Katie arrived at the theater at 5 o'clock, and the play had already began.", 'When she came back home, she found that someone has stolen the diamond ring.']);
add(R, `다음 ⓐ~ⓔ 중, 부사절을 분사구문으로 알맞게 전환한 것을 모두 골라 짝지은 것은?\n\nⓐ When he saw the police, they started to chase him. → Seeing the police, they started to chase him.\nⓑ Since I was sick, I couldn't go to school. → Being sick, I couldn't go to school.\nⓒ While I was walking in the park, I saw an old friend of mine sitting on a bench. → Walking in the park, an old friend of mine saw me sitting on a bench.\nⓓ As I felt really tired, I had to go to bed earlier than usual. → Feeling tired, I had to go to bed earlier than usual.\nⓔ As he read the article, he dropped his cup on the table. → Reading the article, I dropped his cup on the table.`, '4', ['ⓐ, ⓓ', 'ⓐ, ⓔ', 'ⓑ, ⓒ', 'ⓑ, ⓓ', 'ⓑ, ⓓ, ⓔ']);
